    "note": "Comm Sub: 1st Sub. (Buff) H.B. 227, 02-25. Struck \"felony\" and added \"criminal\" in items (vi) and (vii) (Category II restricted person). The House passed this bill 2025-02-25; later amendments are not in the text read. Section 3 is a coordination clause with H.B. 133."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Utah Code 76-10-503): (vi) has been found not guilty by reason of insanity for a criminal offense;\nSection 1 (Utah Code 76-10-503): (vii) has been found mentally incompetent to stand trial for a criminal offense;\nSection 1 (Utah Code 76-10-503): (3) A Category II restricted person who intentionally or knowingly purchases, transfers, possesses, uses, or has under the person's custody or control: (a) a firearm is guilty of a third degree felony; or (b) a dangerous weapon other than a firearm is guilty of a class A misdemeanor."
